# Sales Agent Onboarding Process Assessment

**Purpose:** This questionnaire helps us understand your current process for bringing new sales agents into your organization and providing them with the tools and access they need to be successful.

---

## Section 1: Overview of Your Current Process

**1.1** Please walk us through how you currently bring a new sales agent from their first day to having everything they need to start selling.

**1.2** How long does it typically take from when an agent signs their agreement until they can fully access all necessary systems and start working?
- [ ] Same day
- [ ] 2-3 business days
- [ ] About 1 week
- [ ] 2 weeks or more

**1.3** Which departments or teams are involved in getting a new agent set up?
- [ ] Human Resources
- [ ] Sales Management
- [ ] Information Technology
- [ ] Compliance/Legal
- [ ] Finance/Payroll
- [ ] Training Department
- [ ] Other: ___________

---

## Section 2: Agent Information and Documentation

**2.1** Where do you keep the official records for your sales agents (the "master file" that other systems reference)?
- [ ] Main business system/database
- [ ] HR system (name if known): ___________
- [ ] Sales management system
- [ ] Excel spreadsheets or paper files
- [ ] Information is stored in multiple places

**2.2** What information do you collect when bringing on a new agent?
- [ ] Full legal name
- [ ] Social Security Number/Tax ID
- [ ] Email address
- [ ] Phone number
- [ ] Home address
- [ ] Bank account information (for commission payments)
- [ ] Professional licenses or certifications
- [ ] Background check results
- [ ] Emergency contact information
- [ ] Other: ___________

**2.3** How do you verify that the information provided by new agents is accurate?
- [ ] Review physical documents (driver's license, etc.)
- [ ] Use a background check service
- [ ] Verify professional licenses with state agencies
- [ ] We don't have a formal verification process
- [ ] Other: ___________

---

## Section 3: System Access and Tools

**3.1** What business systems or tools do sales agents need to use in their daily work?
- [ ] Customer relationship management (CRM) system
- [ ] Commission/pay tracking system
- [ ] Training or learning platforms
- [ ] Document storage systems
- [ ] Email and communication tools
- [ ] Sales reporting tools
- [ ] Other: ___________

**3.2** How do new agents get access to these systems?
- [ ] Accounts are created automatically when HR enters their information
- [ ] IT department manually creates accounts
- [ ] Agents can sign up themselves
- [ ] Accounts are created in batches (daily or weekly)
- [ ] Other: ___________

**3.3** How do agents log into these systems?
- [ ] Username and password only
- [ ] Username, password, plus a code sent to their phone
- [ ] Single login that works for all systems
- [ ] ID cards or certificates
- [ ] Fingerprint or other biometric methods
- [ ] Other: ___________

---

## Section 4: What Agents Can Access

**4.1** How do you decide what information and features each agent can access?
- [ ] Based on their role or level (junior vs. senior agent)
- [ ] Based on their sales territory or region
- [ ] Based on what products they sell
- [ ] Their manager must approve their access
- [ ] All agents get the same standard access
- [ ] Other: ___________

**4.2** What business information can sales agents view?
- [ ] Only their own sales and commission information
- [ ] Summary information for their team or territory
- [ ] Customer contact details
- [ ] Product pricing information
- [ ] Historical sales data
- [ ] Other: ___________

**4.3** Do different types of agents have different levels of access?
- [ ] Yes (please describe): ___________
- [ ] No, all agents have the same access

---

## Section 5: Compliance and Legal Requirements

**5.1** What legal or regulatory requirements do you need to follow when onboarding sales agents?
- [ ] Financial reporting requirements (SOX)
- [ ] Industry-specific regulations (please specify): ___________
- [ ] Data privacy laws (GDPR, CCPA, etc.)
- [ ] Professional licensing requirements
- [ ] Background check requirements
- [ ] Other: ___________

**5.2** How often do you review whether agents still need their current level of access?
- [ ] Once per year
- [ ] Every three months
- [ ] When their manager requests a review
- [ ] We don't have a formal review process
- [ ] Other: ___________

**5.3** What records do you keep of agent activities?
- [ ] When accounts are created
- [ ] When agents log into systems
- [ ] What information agents access
- [ ] When access levels are changed
- [ ] We don't keep detailed records
- [ ] Other: ___________

---

## Section 6: When Agents Leave

**6.1** How do you find out when an agent is leaving the company?
- [ ] HR system automatically notifies relevant people
- [ ] Managers send notifications
- [ ] We track contract expiration dates
- [ ] Manual process - someone has to remember to check
- [ ] Other: ___________

**6.2** What happens to an agent's system access when they leave?
- [ ] All access is automatically removed
- [ ] Someone manually removes access from each system
- [ ] Access is gradually reduced over time
- [ ] All access is removed immediately
- [ ] Other: ___________

**6.3** How long do you keep an agent's access active after they leave?
- [ ] Access is removed immediately
- [ ] 30 days
- [ ] 90 days
- [ ] We keep it indefinitely
- [ ] It depends on the situation

---

## Section 7: Current Challenges

**7.1** What are the biggest problems or frustrations with your current onboarding process?
- [ ] Takes too much manual work and time
- [ ] Different systems don't work well together
- [ ] Difficult to meet compliance requirements
- [ ] Agents get frustrated waiting for access
- [ ] Security and data protection concerns
- [ ] Other: ___________

**7.2** Approximately how many new agents do you onboard each month?
- [ ] 1-10
- [ ] 11-50
- [ ] 51-100
- [ ] More than 100

**7.3** What percentage of new agent setups require someone to manually fix problems or handle exceptions?
- [ ] Almost none (0-25%)
- [ ] Some (26-50%)
- [ ] Most (51-75%)
- [ ] Nearly all (76-100%)

---

## Section 8: Your Vision for Improvement

**8.1** What improvements would make the biggest difference in your onboarding process?
- [ ] Faster setup time
- [ ] Agents can do more of the setup themselves
- [ ] Better integration between different systems
- [ ] Stronger security measures
- [ ] Better tracking for compliance purposes
- [ ] Other: ___________

**8.2** Do you have any plans to improve or modernize your current process?
- [ ] Yes, we're already working on improvements
- [ ] Yes, we plan to start next year
- [ ] We're considering it but haven't decided
- [ ] No current plans

**8.3** What would an ideal onboarding process look like for your organization?

